# Memory Bank Policy

This policy defines where to place auto-generated and working markdown notes vs. formal documentation.

## Python Project File Locations

For this project, The Brain MCP, place any Python-related memory_bank files into the `python/memory_bank/` folder.

- Put auto-generated fix/refactor summaries, progress breadcrumbs, and active context notes in `python/memory_bank/`.
- Put plans, specs, design docs, and long-form documentation in `python/docs/`.

## Required Memory Bank Files

Within the `memory_bank/` folder, these files are required (per Thinking Models rules):

- `projectbrief.md`, `techContext.md`, `systemPatterns.md`, `productContext.md`, `activeContext.md`, `progress.md`.

Naming convention for auto-generated entries:

- `YYYY-MM-DD-title.md` (e.g., `2025-08-15-backlog-sync.md`).

If you think the date is before the last entry, ask for clarification. 

Rationale:

- Keeps evolving context lightweight and close to day-to-day work
- Preserves clarity by reserving `docs/` for durable documentation
- Keep minor changes and change details in files within the memory_bank folder. See the Memory Bank Policy for details on organizing working notes and technical implementation details.

- Retain essential files for future reference in `memory_bank/` and its sub-folders.

- Recommended structure:

```text
your-project/
└── memory_bank/
    ├── projectbrief.md
    ├── techContext.md
    ├── systemPatterns.md
    ├── productContext.md
    ├── activeContext.md
    └── progress.md
```

- Recommended structure for the Python version:

```text
your-project/
└── python/
    └──memory_bank/
        ├── projectbrief.md
        ├── techContext.md
        ├── systemPatterns.md
        ├── productContext.md
        ├── activeContext.md
        └── progress.md
```
